# Build output — the binaries are ~57 MB and are rebuilt from source; they belong on a
# Release, never in git history. The packaged forms are listed separately because a DMG or a
# .app can be produced anywhere, not just under dist-bin/.
# ANY dist* directory, not just the two that existed when this was written. `dist-plain/` and
# `dist-shell/` were invented while testing the native shell and were NOT matched, so a
# `git add -A` staged 324 build files and took .git from a few MB to 214 MB in one commit.
/dist*/
/build/
# SwiftPM's output for the native shell — same class as the above.
/macos/.build/
*.spec.bak
*.dmg
*.app/
# NOT a blanket *.whl: vendor/ deliberately commits the SDK wheel, since it is not on PyPI and
# its repo is private. See vendor/README.md.
/wheels/

# Environments
/.venv*/
/venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# notarytool's transcript, written beside the DMG by packaging/sign-macos.sh
notary.txt

# SIGNING KEY MATERIAL. Belongs in ~/.apple-signing (mode 700) and never in a repo — this is
# only a backstop for a mis-typed path. A .p12 carries the Developer ID private key and a .p8 is
# the App Store Connect key; either one in git history means revoking and reissuing.
*.p12
*.p8
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest

# Instance data must NEVER be committed: it holds the owner's knowledge, their people, and
# $AGENTDUET_HOME/.env with a model key and a connector credential.
/.dduet/
/.agentduet-desktop/
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# setuptools build metadata, regenerated on every build
*.egg-info/
# The build stamp the PyInstaller spec writes. It was TRACKED until 2026-08-03 while this
# pattern only matched the repo root, so every build left a tracked file modified and every
# build therefore stamped itself `+dirty` — including builds from a clean commit. That made the
# dirty flag mean nothing, while INSTALL.md tells testers it should never appear.
_build.py

# playwright-mcp screenshots and snapshots — a local debugging aid, never a deliverable
.playwright-mcp/
